"""Local 'as' constructions and asynchronous-programming spellings.

Positive responses mark extent/qualification phrases (especially 'as far as');
negative ones mark role, comparison, and necessity phrases such as 'as part',
'as being', and 'as needed'. Capitalized As strengthens several responses.
Common comparison endings prevent reading the second 'as' as a role marker.
WordNet identifies graded adjectives/adverbs in longer comparisons.
Separate spelling responses cover Async, some medical terms, title labels,
repeated middle dots, and letter-A labels.
Everything else is left near zero; this is not a general semantic parser.
"""

import re
from functools import lru_cache
import wordnet

